From 00fd954fd25cb54559e50b5315197e5c3b322768 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:00:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updates: an update placed by hand is installed only when
 signed or approved on the screen

An update copied to the update folder by hand (over the network, with SSH,
with Kodi's file manager) replaces the whole system at the next start.
Until now the init of a system without Secure Boot installed any such
file without a check, so a changed copy or another build that claims to be
LibreELEC Hades went in silently.

The client of the update channel gains check_update ("hades_update.py
check-update"), which the init of a system without Secure Boot runs before
anything of an update is read: the .tar of a release that the channel of
this system signed, with its signed manifest next to it (check_kept), or
the files, byte for byte and in the init's order, of the approval kept on
this system. The settings add-on looks at the update folder while Kodi
runs and, once a file there has stayed the same for 10 seconds and no
video plays:
- signed: says so in a notification;
- a .tar alone that is the newest release of the channel: it gets the
  name of the manifest and the signed manifest next to it;
- anything else: asks, once per start of Kodi, with "Not now"
  preselected; "Install" approves those bytes and restarts, "Remove it"
  removes it. With Secure Boot no approval is offered: the init takes only
  a signed update, and the message names the installer for Windows.

LibreELEC's behaviour stays one setting away: "Ask before installing an
update placed by hand" (Updates, on by default) off installs any update
without a question; turning it off says what it opens and asks first. A
version chosen from a channel added by hand is approved by the yes to its
question, which now says that LibreELEC Hades did not sign it. A manifest
that was taken before and is gone now is no longer shown as "the newest
version".

Strings 34300-34310 in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx.
